        "original_id": "ebd5a8e2-1dbc-546a-bec6-19655c539671",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: ACRISS, Budget Rent a Car System, Inc.\n- Companies: Avis, Budget, Alamo, National, Enterprise, Europcar, Hertz, Maggiore\n- People: Morris Mirkin\n- Places: Los Angeles, California, Europe, Middle East, Africa\n- Systems: ACRISS Car Classification Code\n- Topics: car rental classification, car rental industry standards\n\nFacts:\n- Budget Rent a Car System, Inc. was founded in 1958 in Los Angeles, California by Morris Mirkin.\n- ACRISS developed and maintains the ACRISS Car Classification Code.\n- The ACRISS Car Classification Code is designed to help customers and travel professionals make informed car rental booking choices in Europe, the Middle East, and Africa.\n- ACRISS is the Association of Car Rental Industry Systems Standards.\n- ACRISS members include Avis, Budget, Alamo, National, Enterprise, Europcar, Hertz, and Maggiore.",
